  "aa_noise": "Qwen advice-off and its identical repeat differed by 8.4 points pooled hinted (30.1% versus 38.6%) and by 6 to 11 points per seed; Gemma repeat matched exactly.",
  "oracle": "The oracle arm (native ARC with a pool larger than every stored token, so nothing is evicted) reached 0% on Gemma but 15.7% on Qwen, above reachable-hold at 10.8%. Qwen oracle losses are therefore not evictions; they fit the pinned vLLM hybrid lookup effect found in the decide round, where a quick return with a GPU full-attention hit lacking Mamba state discards a complete CPU copy. Per seed reachable-hold was 25, 8 and 4% against the oracle 23, 23 and 6%; the seed-308 gap (15 points) exceeds that seed A/A difference (10 points) and is unexplained, so the oracle is not an upper bound for Qwen in this setup."
 }
